<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="zones_manager.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="zones_manager">
    <!-- P3 track-A: the zones manager (game::zones_manager, the `Y` screen). A
         right-docked panel mirroring list_items: a header ("Zones manager"), a
         scrolling list of nearby (or all) zones — each row a coloured name, type,
         distance/direction cluster and a vehicle marker, the active row
         recoloured — the active zone's options block (key→value descriptions),
         and a multi-line shortcut footer whose <O> overlay / <G> submap-grid
         tokens are live-coloured by state. Render-only: the keyboard owns
         add/remove/enable/disable/move/edit and the overlay toggles; the map
         cursor + zone overlay stay on the map path. Synced each frame from
         zones/active_index; hidden during the nested point-selection look_around
         (the curses `show` gate). Per-segment colour baked via cata_text_to_rml. -->
    <div class="panel zm-panel">
        <div class="zm-header" data-rml="header_rml"></div>
        <div id="zm-list" class="zm-list scroll-pane">
            <div data-if="empty" class="zm-empty" data-rml="empty_rml"></div>
            <div class="zm-row" data-for="r : rows" data-class-selected="r.selected">
                <span class="zm-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                <span class="zm-type" data-rml="r.type_rml"></span>
                <span class="zm-dist" data-rml="r.dist_rml"></span>
                <span class="zm-veh" data-rml="r.veh_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="zm-options" data-if="has_options">
            <div class="zm-options-title" data-rml="options_title_rml"></div>
            <div class="zm-opt" data-for="o : options">
                <span class="zm-opt-key" data-rml="o.key_rml"></span>
                <span class="zm-opt-val" data-rml="o.val_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="zm-footer" data-rml="footer_rml"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
